    {
      "id": "ce5319c56d129fda9b58bdea980ff3f5d929667b",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 465423757,
          "type": null,
          "body": "[The detailed description of `QTemporaryFile`](https://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qtemporaryfile.html#details) says:\n\n> A temporary file will have some static part of the name and some part that is calculated to be unique. The default filename will be determined from [QCoreApplication::applicationName](https://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qcoreapplication.html#applicationName-prop)() (otherwise `qt_temp`) and will be placed into the temporary path as returned by [QDir::tempPath](https://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qdir.html#tempPath)(). If you specify your own filename, a relative file path will not be placed in the temporary directory by default, but be relative to the current working directory.\n\nso I guess `QTemporaryFile()` (i.e., with no arguments) will automatically give you a temporary file in the temporary directory.  Otherwise, yes, you have to make sure the template is a full pathname that includes the temporary directory.",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
          "created_at": "2020-12-12T00:20:08.706Z",
          "updated_at": "2020-12-12T00:21:52.590Z",
